{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Ccy2MQwkmHQk9Syq4JR9z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The implementation is complete and verified — the project runs with zero compile errors. Here's what I did.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe Mushroom Jump Pad was an `Area3D` with an empty script (`extends Area3D`) and no behavior. I implemented the full spec in `jumping_pad/jumping_pad.gd`.\n\n**How it fits the existing game:** The pad is a detection-only `Area3D` (no solid body), and the player (`CharacterBody3D`) drives itself with `velocity` + `move_and_slide()`. So the natural, physics-correct way to launch is to overwrite the player's velocity and let its own physics loop carry the motion.\n\nEach spec requirement maps to the code:\n\n1. **Instant physics launch** — `body_entered` fires on contact and sets `player.velocity`. Because it's a real velocity change fed through the player's `move_and_slide()`, ceiling/wall collisions mid-flight still resolve naturally (no scripted position animation).\n2. **Powerful** — `launch_speed = 30.0` vs. the normal `jump_initial_impulse = 12.0`; with gravity −30 that's ~15 m of height vs. ~2.5 m for a max jump.\n3. **Momentum reset + air control** — velocity is *overwritten* (not added to), so arrival speed never carries through; the player's `_physics_process` still applies horizontal input every frame, preserving midair steering.\n4. **Launches along the surface normal** — direction is `global_transform.basis.y`, so a flat pad throws straight up and a slope-tilted pad throws up-and-outward.\n5. **Cap squash-and-wobble** — the mushroom mesh (a single unit) is instantly squashed (flatten Y, widen XZ), then a `TRANS_ELASTIC / EASE_OUT` tween springs it back, overshooting past rest with a rubbery wobble before settling. Any prior tween is killed first, so every contact restarts the animation from scratch.\n6. **Player-only** — guarded by `if not body is Player: return`, so enemies (`RigidBody3D`), boxes, grenades, and bullets pass through with no launch or reaction.\n\nLaunch strength, squash depth, and rebound time are all `@export`ed for easy tuning. Nothing else in the game was touched."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":207,"cache_read_input_tokens":35038,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":207,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"edfbf184-0857-4705-b334-06689a2545a2","uuid":"9af60400-af8a-4264-b6eb-73ebede7f197","request_id":"req_011Ccy2MQ2w5h1DxhEhfFSRq"}
